Jarvis-hermes
=============

This project builds on the following open-source work.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
jarvis_ai — https://github.com/eadmin2/jarvis_ai
MIT License, Copyright (c) eadmin2
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Jarvis-hermes extends jarvis_ai's voice pipeline and HUD. Specifically:

- `gpu-node/stt_server.py` is a Linux/CUDA rewrite of upstream's
  `worker/stt_server.py`. The HTTP contract (POST /stt taking raw int16
  16 kHz mono PCM, returning {"text": ...}) is kept identical so upstream's
  voice server works against it unmodified. The Windows DLL-loading shim was
  removed, defaults changed to large-v3 + Thai, and health/stat reporting
  added.

- `gpu-node/worker_stats.py` follows upstream's `worker/worker_stats.py`
  contract for the HUD "machines" panel, extended with per-sidecar health.

- `host/config/server.example.yaml` is derived from upstream's
  `server/config/server.example.yaml`, with the stt.remote and voice blocks
  changed for this deployment.

Everything else in this repository — the Thai TTS sidecar (`tts_server.py`),
the host-side F5-TTS provider, the installer, systemd units, scripts, and all
documentation — is original work.

